  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Barbados is implementing the Decent Work Country Programme 2025&#x2013;2030, which includes priorities on labour legislation reform, occupational safety and health, the informal economy and social protection. Informal employment remains significant and is particularly prevalent in services, tourism and domestic work, where workers can face barriers to representation, effective access to rights and social protection. During the biennium, the International Labour Organization works to strengthen workers&#x2019; organizations&#x2019; capacity to attract and represent new groups of workers and to improve their services. The strategy supports three areas of change: stronger trade union participation in the planning, implementation and monitoring of the national Decent Work Country Programme; a just transition learning module, to strengthen outreach and awareness among union members and the wider public; and strengthened support for domestic workers through the development and dissemination of a model employment contract and practical guidance on complaints mechanisms. Women, young people and workers in vulnerable situations benefit through improved access to information, representation and support services.</narrative>
  </description>
